      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since your pediatrician is unavailable, you should use an oral rehydration solution like Pedialyte, not diluted apple juice, as the correct electrolyte balance is crucial. If he is only drowsy and still responsive, try offering small, frequent sips of Pedialyte to combat dehydration. However, if his sleepiness worsens, or if you notice any signs of lethargy, vomiting, or fever, you must seek urgent care immediately.",
